{"content_hash": "0be2409426ce4bb4", "version_id": 165, "article_id": 17, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "How the 2026 Nature Index infectious-disease tables were built", "title_zh": "2026年《自然指数》传染病榜单是怎么算出来的", "topic": "science", "source": "nature", "source_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02999-z", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52462408254_7688613222_b.jpg", "credit": "DCHNwam · pdm 1.0 · via flickr"}, "published_date": "2026-10-07", "word_count": 211, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "A new methodology guide explains how Nature Spotlight's 2026 infectious-disease rankings were assembled, drawing on the Nature Index database and a keyword search of Digital Science's Dimensions platform.", "lead_zh": "一份新发布的方法说明解释了《自然》2026年传染病专题榜单是如何编制的——数据来自自然指数数据库，并对Digital Science旗下的Dimensions平台进行了关键词检索。", "preview": "The tables underpinning the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases derive from the Nature Index database, encompassing infectious-diseas", "preview_zh": "2026年《自然》专题“传染病”所依据的榜单，源自自然指数数据库，涵盖2021年至2025年间发表在自然科学与健康科学期刊上的传染病论文。这份方法说明于2026年10月7日发布，详细交代了榜单的编制方式，让读者清楚了解所采用的评判标准。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 155, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/audio/17/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 102.525, "size_bytes": 618912, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 241, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/data/versions/165.json", "paragraphs": ["The tables underpinning the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases derive from the Nature Index database, encompassing infectious-disease papers that appeared in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025. The methodology note, published on 7 October 2026, sets out precisely how the ranking was compiled, offering readers a transparent account of the criteria applied.", "To isolate relevant articles, researchers ran a keyword search across abstracts and titles in Dimensions, the bibliometric database operated by Digital Science—itself part of Holtzbrinck, the majority shareholder of Nature's publisher, Springer Nature. The search spanned 83 infectious diseases and incorporated five subcategories to capture severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes, mirroring the parameters used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious disease tables.", "Only Dimensions records that also featured in the Nature Index database were retained, and these constituted the final data set behind the Spotlight's tables. The supplement, the note stresses, is editorially independent, with advertisers exercising no influence over its content—a caveat that underscores the publication's commitment to editorial integrity.", "The guide arrives amid a flurry of related coverage, from pandemic preparedness and Ebola frontline care to emerging research on gut microbes, hepatitis B and early flu seasons. Together, these pieces illustrate how infectious-disease science continues to command urgent attention across clinical, epidemiological and policy domains."], "paragraphs_zh": ["2026年《自然》专题“传染病”所依据的榜单，源自自然指数数据库，涵盖2021年至2025年间发表在自然科学与健康科学期刊上的传染病论文。这份方法说明于2026年10月7日发布，详细交代了榜单的编制方式，让读者清楚了解所采用的评判标准。", "为了筛出相关文章，研究人员在Dimensions的摘要和标题中进行了关键词检索。Dimensions是Digital Science运营的文献计量数据库，而Digital Science隶属于霍尔茨布林克——后者是《自然》出版方施普林格·自然的大股东。检索覆盖83种传染病，并纳入5个子类以涵盖严重冠状病毒和流感亚型，参数与2021年自然指数传染病榜单保持一致。", "只有同时被自然指数数据库收录的Dimensions记录才会被保留，这些记录构成了专题榜单的最终数据集。说明特别强调，该增刊在编辑上独立运作，广告商对其内容没有任何影响力——这一声明凸显了出版方对编辑独立性的坚持。", "这份指南发布之际，相关报道层出不穷，涉及大流行病防范、埃博拉前线护理，以及肠道微生物、乙肝和流感季提前等新兴研究。这些内容共同表明，传染病科学在临床、流行病学和政策领域依然备受关注、刻不容缓。"], "body": "The tables underpinning the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases derive from the Nature Index database, encompassing infectious-disease papers that appeared in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025. The methodology note, published on 7 October 2026, sets out precisely how the ranking was compiled, offering readers a transparent account of the criteria applied.\n\nTo isolate relevant articles, researchers ran a keyword search across abstracts and titles in Dimensions, the bibliometric database operated by Digital Science—itself part of Holtzbrinck, the majority shareholder of Nature's publisher, Springer Nature. The search spanned 83 infectious diseases and incorporated five subcategories to capture severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes, mirroring the parameters used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious disease tables.\n\nOnly Dimensions records that also featured in the Nature Index database were retained, and these constituted the final data set behind the Spotlight's tables. The supplement, the note stresses, is editorially independent, with advertisers exercising no influence over its content—a caveat that underscores the publication's commitment to editorial integrity.\n\nThe guide arrives amid a flurry of related coverage, from pandemic preparedness and Ebola frontline care to emerging research on gut microbes, hepatitis B and early flu seasons. Together, these pieces illustrate how infectious-disease science continues to command urgent attention across clinical, epidemiological and policy domains.", "body_zh": "2026年《自然》专题“传染病”所依据的榜单，源自自然指数数据库，涵盖2021年至2025年间发表在自然科学与健康科学期刊上的传染病论文。这份方法说明于2026年10月7日发布，详细交代了榜单的编制方式，让读者清楚了解所采用的评判标准。\n\n为了筛出相关文章，研究人员在Dimensions的摘要和标题中进行了关键词检索。Dimensions是Digital Science运营的文献计量数据库，而Digital Science隶属于霍尔茨布林克——后者是《自然》出版方施普林格·自然的大股东。检索覆盖83种传染病，并纳入5个子类以涵盖严重冠状病毒和流感亚型，参数与2021年自然指数传染病榜单保持一致。\n\n只有同时被自然指数数据库收录的Dimensions记录才会被保留，这些记录构成了专题榜单的最终数据集。说明特别强调，该增刊在编辑上独立运作，广告商对其内容没有任何影响力——这一声明凸显了出版方对编辑独立性的坚持。\n\n这份指南发布之际，相关报道层出不穷，涉及大流行病防范、埃博拉前线护理，以及肠道微生物、乙肝和流感季提前等新兴研究。这些内容共同表明，传染病科学在临床、流行病学和政策领域依然备受关注、刻不容缓。", "text": "The tables underpinning the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases derive from the Nature Index database, encompassing infectious-disease papers that appeared in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025. The methodology note, published on 7 October 2026, sets out precisely how the ranking was compiled, offering readers a transparent account of the criteria applied. To isolate relevant articles, researchers ran a keyword search across abstracts and titles in Dimensions, the bibliometric database operated by Digital Science—itself part of Holtzbrinck, the majority shareholder of Nature's publisher, Springer Nature. The search spanned 83 infectious diseases and incorporated five subcategories to capture severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes, mirroring the parameters used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious disease tables. Only Dimensions records that also featured in the Nature Index database were retained, and these constituted the final data set behind the Spotlight's tables. The supplement, the note stresses, is editorially independent, with advertisers exercising no influence over its content—a caveat that underscores the publication's commitment to editorial integrity. The guide arrives amid a flurry of related coverage, from pandemic preparedness and Ebola frontline care to emerging research on gut microbes, hepatitis B and early flu seasons. Together, these pieces illustrate how infectious-disease science continues to command urgent attention across clinical, epidemiological and policy domains.", "vocab": [{"word": "underpin", "pos": "verb", "zh": "构成……的基础；支撑", "note": "常用于抽象事物，如数据支撑结论。"}, {"word": "encompass", "pos": "verb", "zh": "涵盖；包含", "note": "比 include 更正式，强调范围广。"}, {"word": "bibliometric", "pos": "adj", "zh": "文献计量的", "note": "学术出版领域常用词。"}, {"word": "subcategory", "pos": "noun", "zh": "子类别", "note": "分类讨论时常用。"}, {"word": "retain", "pos": "verb", "zh": "保留；留存", "note": "数据筛选语境中很常见。"}, {"word": "constitute", "pos": "verb", "zh": "构成；组成", "note": "正式用语，后接名词。"}, {"word": "caveat", "pos": "noun", "zh": "警告；限制性说明", "note": "常指附带条件的提醒。"}, {"word": "underscore", "pos": "verb", "zh": "强调；凸显", "note": "新闻英语高频词。"}, {"word": "editorial integrity", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "编辑独立性/操守", "note": "媒体行业固定搭配。"}, {"word": "flurry", "pos": "noun", "zh": "一阵；一连串", "note": "a flurry of 后接复数名词。"}, {"word": "pandemic preparedness", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "大流行病防范", "note": "公共卫生领域术语。"}, {"word": "epidemiological", "pos": "adj", "zh": "流行病学的", "note": "与流行病学相关。"}, {"word": "command attention", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "引起关注", "note": "command 此处意为“博得”。"}, {"word": "transparent", "pos": "adj", "zh": "透明的；公开的", "note": "常形容流程或说明。"}], "title_original": "A guide to Nature Index tables", "summary_original": "Nature, Published online: 07 October 2026;\ndoi:10.1038/d41586-026-02999-z\nInformation on the methodology used in the ranking for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases.", "body_original": "SPOTLIGHT\n07 October 2026\nA guide to Nature Index tables\nInformation on the methodology used in the ranking for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases.\nEmail\nBluesky\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nReddit\nWhatsapp\nX\nSave article\nView saved research\nThe tables for the 2026\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\nare based on the\nNature Index database\nand cover infectious-disease articles published in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025.\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\nA keyword search on abstracts and titles was conducted to extract infectious-disease articles in Digital Science’s Dimensions database (Digital Science is part of Holtzbrinck, the majority shareholder of\nNature\n’s publisher, Springer Nature). The search covered 83 infectious diseases and included 5 subcategories to cover severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes. The\ndiseases and their Dimensions search strings\nwere the same as those for\nNature Index 2021 Infectious disease\n. The Dimensions articles identified that were also in the Nature Index database formed the data set for the tables in this Spotlight.\nEnjoying our latest content?\nLog in or create an account to continue\nAccess the most recent journalism from Nature's award-winning team\nExplore the latest features & opinion covering groundbreaking research\nAccess through your institution\nor\nSign in or create an account\nContinue with Google\nContinue with ORCiD\ndoi: https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-02999-z\nThis article is part of\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\n, an editorially independent supplement. Advertisers have no influence over the content.\nRelated Articles\n‘When prevention disappears, infections rise’: can the world still end AIDS?\nWhy we must advocate for proper care on the frontlines of the Ebola outbreak\nWhy sound, strong science alone isn’t enough in pandemic preparedness\nPartner content: The microbial sleuths tracking the rise of drug resistant bacteria\nPartner content: Investigating the next generation of RNA vaccines\nPartner content: The burden of infectious disease in China is shifting\nPartner content: Preparing for the next major disease outbreak\nPartner content: Big hospital, bigger ideas for pandemic preparedness\nPartner content: Zika research points the way to flavivirus antivirals\nSubjects\nDiseases\nInfection\nPublic health\nLatest on:\nDiseases\nInfection\nPublic health\nWhy sound, strong science alone isn’t enough in pandemic preparedness\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nWhy we must advocate for proper care on the frontlines of the Ebola outbreak\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nRevealed: how this common gut microbe protects against heart disease\nNews\n07 OCT 26\nFlu season could kick off ‘incredibly’ early — what scientists are watching\nNews\n06 OCT 26\n‘Epigenetic’ editing is here: gene-tagging technique banishes hepatitis B virus\nNews\n21 SEP 26\n‘Stomach bugs’ send protective immune cells rushing from gut to brain\nNews\n15 SEP 26\n‘When prevention disappears, infections rise’: can the world still end AIDS?\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nWhy sound, strong science alone isn’t enough in pandemic preparedness\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nFlu season could kick off ‘incredibly’ early — what scientists are watching\nNews\n06 OCT 26\nJobs\nFaculty Positions at the Center for Machine Learning Research (CMLR), Peking University\nCMLR's goal is to advance machine learning-related research across a wide range of disciplines.\nBeijing (CN)\nCenter for Machine Learning Research (CMLR), Peking University\nAssistant or Associate Professor of Cell Biology\nDepartment of Cell Biology at the University of Virginia School of Medicine invites applications for Assistant or Associate Professor of Cell Biology\nCharlottesville, Virginia\nUniversity of Virginia\nRecruitment Announcement for High-Level Talent at the Center for Agricultural Microbiology\nJoin HZAU's global faculty team to advance research with competitive benefits.\nWuhan, Hubei (CN)\nHuazhong Agricultural University (HZAU)\nOpen-Rank Faculty Position in Theoretical Biology\nThe Department of Biological Sciences seeks an outstanding individual for an open-rank faculty position in Theoretical Biology.\nNashville, Tennessee\nVanderbilt University Department of Biological Sciences\nProteomics Specialist\nBuild the science that shapes the future of human health. Application closing date: 08 November 2026 Join a place where ambitious science thrives...\nMilan (IT)\nHuman Technopole", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T01:10:35.574348", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.263, "sm": 100, "em": 262, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "tables", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.725, "sm": 275, "em": 725, "cs": 4, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "underpinning", "s": 0.738, "e": 1.263, "sm": 737, "em": 1262, "cs": 11, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "the", "s": 1.275, "e": 1.362, "sm": 1275, "em": 1362, "cs": 24, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "2026", "s": 1.375, "e": 2.35, "sm": 1375, "em": 2350, "cs": 28, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Nature", "s": 2.362, "e": 2.737, "sm": 2362, "em": 2737, "cs": 33, "ce": 39, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "Spotlight", "s": 2.75, "e": 3.362,